  "2026-08-22T02:01:59.814Z","harness:codex","Reviewed delivery evidence: PR #1083 merged exact reviewed head 4b5f645d3e2ff1e4de1d00eccfbc158f1eb9f3ee into main as e790cd0e12c2907998bcca8797c7ae3577f28d8f. All required exact-head hosted checks passed; the review inventory had zero unresolved threads after every actionable finding was fixed or evidence-backed declined, every bot comment received an explicit usefulness reaction, and the manual CodeRabbit rerun was rate-limited. Greptile was explicitly triggered but produced no check, review, or comment, so provider silence is recorded as a limitation rather than approval. Final packed-artifact verification passed from a fresh temporary consumer under Node and Bun with UTF-8 ceilings and corrective-action preservation. Full repository coverage passed 551 files and 7,721 tests at exact 100/100/100/100. This item returns to open and unclaimed because its documented exhaustive residual remains outside this delivered tranche."
  "2026-08-22T02:49:35.611Z","harness:codex","Release evidence 2026-08-22: production Auto Release run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/32545649142 completed successfully and created immutable-source tag v2026.8.22 at d7b6f18ce912ccf84d754cf5e539b4090c62c98b. Tag-driven Release run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/32546288241 completed successfully, published npm @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.22 with provenance, created the non-draft/non-prerelease GitHub release, finalized Sentry release pm-cli@2026.8.22 with 18 commits and zero new groups, and uploaded sourcemaps. Public verification passed GitHub/npm plus fresh npx and Bun 11-step installed-agent sessions; one first-attempt post-success temporary cleanup race was retried successfully and its known residual directory was safely removed. Post-release Sentry shows zero unresolved issues; the 14-day gate reports critical=0, high=0, ignored_noise=0, and ignored_expected_handled=0. Telemetry flush delivered 3/3 valid events with queue_progressed=true, queue_empty=true, zero invalid rows, and no failed flush. GitHub reports isImmutable=false, so immutability is policy/workflow-enforced through the exact tag SHA rather than platform-enforced. The item remains open and unclaimed for its already documented residual."
  "2026-08-22T04:33:17.474Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-22: replace the partial hand-maintained refusal sample with contract-derived closed-domain, subcommand, required-argument, and mutually-exclusive probes; execute advertised recovery and ratchet closure plus error-code reachability. Duplicate check used the complete 2,533-item all-status corpus."
  "2026-08-22T04:35:55.216Z","harness:codex","TDD negative evidence: the first contract probe found that 'pm schema nonsense --json' did not refuse an unknown subcommand; it registered a custom type through an undocumented positional shorthand. The accidental type was immediately removed with 'pm schema remove-type nonsense --json'; no schema definition remains. The append-only workspace history preserves both operations. This tranche will make schema action parsing conform to its declared subcommand domain and add the case to executable refusal closure."
  "2026-08-22T06:05:51.111Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence 2026-08-22: the refusal gate now executes 117/117 isolated wrong-invocation contracts at closure_fraction=1.0: 18 closed-domain and mutual-exclusion cases, 88 required positional omissions derived from the public grammar, seven authoritative positional-action families, and four tracker preflight states. Every grammar refusal proves usage exit, stable code, complete action domain where applicable, executable help recovery, and a before/after semantic tracker hash. The public refusal envelope carries surface, rejected value when observable, legal domain when known, and exit code; atomic retry argv survives diagnostic compaction. The schema typo negative control proves lowercase unknown actions cannot mutate custom types while explicit and PascalCase type creation remain supported. Gate and scorer negative controls cover missing/unexpected probes, code/domain/exit drift, dead recovery, mutation, ratchet shrinkage, malformed preflight, and diagnostic over-budget/action loss. Verification: standalone refusal gate passed 117/117 plus diagnostics 10/10; focused 23/23 passed; full repository coverage passed 553 files and 7,732 tests at exact 100 percent statements, branches, functions, and lines; full lint/static assurance, contracts, SDK surface, security scan, dependency audit, packed artifact, npx, and clean temporary npm and Bun consumers passed."
  "2026-08-22T06:13:06.919Z","harness:codex","Tranche boundary 2026-08-22: this PR completes grammar-derived required-argument and closed-action coverage, strengthens the refusal envelope, and raises the executable ratchet from 22 to 117 probes. The feature remains open because its literal acceptance text still requires a complete census of every closed-domain flag and declared error-code reachability, including explicit reporting for codes without an executable wrong-invocation producer. Those residuals are not inferred complete from the passing grammar corpus."
