  "2026-08-22T06:27:23.414Z","harness:codex","Hosted smoke remediation evidence: exact head af6c642f7 exposed the intentional failing-command envelope expansion as 219 estimated tokens versus the published 200-token ceiling. pnpm quality:agent-task-token:update ratcheted only that scenario from 200 to 219 and the composite from 2178 to 2197; small-workspace 552, large-workspace 1055, and returning-agent 371 remained unchanged. pnpm quality:agent-task-token passed, and node scripts/release/agent-task-token-gate.mjs --negative-control still detected the seeded million-token regression. The feature remains open because the literal acceptance residual is still the complete declared flag/mutual-exclusion/error-code reachability census."
  "2026-08-22T06:34:47.629Z","harness:codex","Hosted review remediation evidence: four confirmed CodeRabbit findings are fixed. Parsed closed domains now survive context merging into recovery.allowed_values and refusal.legal_domain; assurance missing-argument refusals identify kind, preset, owner, assertion-id, gate-id, or id through required and recovery.missing; the missing-owner path has a distinct regression; MergeSubcommand is exported from both public SDK barrels and the owned surface snapshot. Focused 64 tests, typecheck, ESLint, contracts:check, sdk:surface:check, the 117/117 refusal closure gate, the unchanged 2197-token task entitlement, and package-owned changelog check pass. The generated changelog wording and report-finding catalog suggestions were verified but intentionally not hand-edited: CHANGELOG.md is package-owned and unchanged by its generator, while code-named scorer findings follow the existing PmRefusalClosureFinding and tracker-preflight public catalog convention."
  "2026-08-22T06:45:06.859Z","harness:codex","Reviewed tranche receipt 2026-08-22: PR #1086 merged exact reviewed head 474fcbd492584b6df5853ddf546f22ff7e13bfa7 into main as 5d1110d5c5fa9e5c82b4638220fe7fafcec14a78. All required exact-head hosted checks passed and zero review threads remain unresolved. This merged tranche raises executable closure to 117/117 current obligations with a versioned ratchet and negative controls. Honest residual is unchanged: the feature remains open until a complete contract-declared census covers every closed-domain flag and mutual exclusion and every declared error code is proven reachable or explicitly reported unreachable. Fresh CodeRabbit rerun rate limiting, Sourcery quota exhaustion, and Cubic skip are provider limitations, not approvals."
  "2026-08-22T07:18:10.623Z","harness:codex","Live recurrence 2026-08-22: pm-xam9bt records a current producer whose restore text says to increase a 4,500-token effective budget while its executable CLI binding recommends 1,200. This is now a typed blocked_by edge and a recurs_from link to closed pm-h8tpeh. Recovery closure must measure monotonic progress and cycle freedom, not only command parseability or one-step execution."
  "2026-08-23T06:39:16.461Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-23: active in the same SDK-first tranche to compose the generated error catalog, reachability declarations, closed-domain constraints, positional grammar, and executable refusal corpus into a complete closure census. Existing closed pm-elmpav, pm-x4nn3z, and pm-h8tpeh are reused rather than duplicated."
  "2026-08-23T07:03:26.511Z","harness:codex","Progress: complete 333-code emitted catalog now joins owned-state, 18 closed-domain, and 95 grammar probes. The generated census reports 13 executable codes and all 320 uncovered obligations explicitly, with a no-regression executable-code ratchet; this is an honest incremental closure tranche, not completion of the feature."
  "2026-08-23T07:10:41.912Z","harness:codex","Focused verification: refusal-closure gate unit suite passed its real 117-probe process corpus in 70.2s and reports catalog_closure={catalog:333, executable:13, uncovered:320, ratchet:13/13}; generated REFUSAL_CLOSURE_CENSUS.md restores every uncovered code."
