  "2026-08-23T08:50:11.412Z","harness:codex","Reviewed incremental delivery: PR #1096 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1096 carries the complete 333-code census and 13-code ratchet. This umbrella remains open and unclaimed with all 320 uncovered codes listed explicitly."
  "2026-08-23T10:17:07.276Z","harness:codex","Review tranche evidence: CodeRabbit finding 3838168906 is addressed with a canonical executable error-code identity ratchet in addition to the existing count ratchet. The gate now fails when an executable code is swapped while the count remains 13. Current live census remains intentionally incomplete: 13 executable rows out of 333 catalog codes, 320 uncovered, while all 12 canonical compatibility groups are present and 117/117 executable recovery probes close. Focused census and gate tests, generated-surface checks, pnpm lint, pnpm quality:static, and exact 100% coverage all pass. This feature remains open for the remaining 320 catalog codes."
  "2026-08-23T12:34:39.207Z","harness:codex","Review recurrence start: CodeRabbit findings 3838502157 and 3838502163 are accepted after live validation; link the referenced refusal test file and make generated census row ordering locale-independent."
  "2026-08-23T13:11:28.577Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: linked tests/integration/refusal-reachability.integration.spec.ts so every recorded runnable test path resolves, replaced locale-sensitive census ordering with code-unit ordering, and proved both comparator paths at the direct SDK boundary. Focused census tests pass 5/5; pnpm lint and the full static assurance chain pass; final coverage passes 7,848 tests across 566 files at exact 100% statements 57,373/57,373, branches 42,920/42,920, functions 11,948/11,948, and lines 55,304/55,304. The umbrella remains open because the honest live census still has 320 explicit uncovered catalog rows."
  "2026-08-23T13:35:09.763Z","harness:codex","Correction to the 2026-08-23T13:11:28.577Z evidence comment: the live baseline contains 13 executable code rows across 12 canonical compatibility groups, not 13 executable compatibility groups. This append-only correction preserves the original history event and the reviewed row-versus-group distinction."
  "2026-08-23T13:47:05.971Z","harness:codex","Terminal review evidence: census receipt counts now include only closed-domain and grammar contracts whose error codes join the catalog; the foreign-input negative control proves one accepted and one discarded contract report count 1 for each family. The append-only wording correction records 13 executable code rows across 12 canonical compatibility groups. Focused tests pass 31/31, full coverage passes 7,848 tests across 566 files at exact 100/100/100/100, and pnpm lint/static assurance passes."
  "2026-08-23T20:29:27.954Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-23: actively extend the complete 333-code closure census only for the new bulk-id/file-input and preview refusal producers introduced in this branch. The existing 13 executable rows/12 compatibility groups and 320 explicit uncovered rows are the live baseline; this tranche will advance rather than overstate the umbrella."
  "2026-08-23T22:05:19.500Z","harness:codex","Bounded closure-census tranche evidence 2026-08-24: the three new bulk ID source failures are owned, executable, catalogued producers with real-process probes and generated recovery documentation. The live census advances from 333 catalog / 13 executable rows / 12 canonical groups to 336 catalog / 16 executable rows / 15 canonical groups while retaining 117/117 grammar/refusal probe closure and explicitly listing the unchanged 320 uncovered obligations. Ratchet, catalog, negative-control, generated-surface, 7,858-test exact 100% coverage, and full lint/static assurance pass. This is not item-wide completion; the umbrella remains open for the 320 explicit uncovered codes."
  "2026-08-25T08:44:59.149Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-25: actively advancing the canonical complete error-code census through the same manifest-diagnostics vertical slice. The live baseline is 336 catalog codes, 16 executable rows across 15 canonical groups, 320 explicit uncovered obligations, and 117/117 executable grammar probes; this branch will add contract-owned real-process evidence for manifest author diagnostics without claiming unrelated uncovered codes."
  "2026-08-25T09:51:05.168Z","harness:codex","Progress evidence 2026-08-25: the producer-derived refusal census now executes real health process paths for manifest_unknown_key and no_version_bounds_declared. The ratchet advances from 16 to 18 executable error codes and from 15 to 17 required canonical groups while retaining the published v1 constants as compatibility aliases. The focused PM linked run passed 16/16 tests, the standalone recovery gate passed 117/117 obligations and 10/10 diagnostic budgets, and exact full coverage passed 7,906 tests at 100/100/100/100. Catalog closure remains intentionally incomplete: 342 declared codes, 18 executable, 324 uncovered (5.2632%); this umbrella stays open for later producer groups rather than claiming false completion."
learnings[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-19T05:28:38.341Z","harness:codex","Executable assurance should run the full real corpus once, then exercise failure classification through deterministic injected observations. Replaying an expensive corpus for each scorer branch adds latency without improving behavioral evidence."
  "2026-08-19T08:39:06.383Z","harness:codex","Adapter-only enumerable options can silently defeat SDK fast paths even when behavior remains correct. Pin the real CLI registration path against corrupted source files so derived-index use is observable, and treat raw Commander negation defaults as non-semantic only after normalized filters preserve requested fallback semantics."
  "2026-08-19T18:27:49.965Z","harness:codex",Recovery metrics stay trustworthy only when executable linked tests evolve with repository structure and the umbrella distinguishes completed tranches from residual scope.
  "2026-08-21T23:59:02.159Z","harness:codex",A recovery-closure corpus must validate both the presence of a recovery object and a usable corrective action. Negative controls for missing actions and forged/inconsistent degradation receipts prevent superficially structured diagnostics from passing.
  "2026-08-25T09:51:05.386Z","harness:codex","When a new executable refusal group raises a public ratchet, add a versioned baseline export and retain the prior export unchanged; classify advisory lint findings by their emitted process exit class rather than assuming every invalid manifest signal is a usage error."
